    "title": "Rocket launch from Vandenberg Space Force Base seen across California",
    "text": "CALIFORNIARocket launch from Vandenberg Space Force Base seen across Coachella Valley and California Eric HartleyPalm Springs Desert SunSept. 14, 2023Updated Sept. 15, 2023, 12:16 a.m. PTA rocket launch from Vandenberg Space Force Base was visible across much of Southern California, including the Coachella Valley, on Thursday night.The takeoff at 7:27 p.m. was of by the private company Firefly Aerospace's Alpha launch vehicle, the space news site NSF reported.The Space Force did not immediately announce the launch, but NSF reported the military branch contracted with Firefly to do the launch as part of a test of the nation's ability to put a satellite into orbit immediately in case of an emergency.Vandenberg, a base on the California coast in Santa Barbara County, is about 150 miles west of Los Angeles and 300 miles from the Coachella Valley.According to news reports and social media posts, the rocket could be seen from Arizona and the Las Vegas area, too.Investors Scrambling Before Starlink Goes PublicLearn About The Clever Way Everyday Folks Are Getting Exposure Before It Goes PublicProfitable News | AdAdLearn MoreUndo12 Things To Cut When Living On RetirementGreensprout | AdAdUndo10 Stocks in the Defense Spending BoomSee Which 10 Defense Stocks Show Strong Growth Signals.Seeking Alpha | AdAdRead MoreUndoCompare Missouri Car Insurance Before Auto-RenewingA quick comparison before auto insurance renewal could make a real difference.FinanceBuzz | AdAdUndoMissouri Low Mileage Drivers Could Pay Less For Auto InsuranceCheck how much you could save on car insurance.FinanceBuzz | AdAdUndo12 Things To Cut When Living On Retirement IncomeGreensprout | AdAdUndoRIU Week is here! Choose your hotel from 95$Take advantage of RIU Week’s irresistible prices. Also, as a RIU Class member, you’ll enjoy free airport transfers and special perks.RIU Hotels | AdAdBook NowUndoBehind-The-Scenes Facts About The MunstersOutdoor Revival | AdAdUndoThousands of Timeshare Owners Ar